SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari’s Speech at the 4th National Summit on Diminishing Corruption in the Public Sector","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-10-04","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buharis-speech-at-the-4th-national-summit-on-diminishing-corruption-in-the-public-sector/","claim":"Buhari said fighting corruption remained a cardinal pillar of the administration, linked the Open Government Partnership to transparency in public finances and procurement, and said ICPC should continue investigating sexual harassment in educational institutions.","locator":"paras. 3-4 and 18-19 of the speech","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_low","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential transcript; reliable for what he said, but self-report and not independent proof of practice.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari statement; strong attribution for rhetoric and commitments, weak for actual adherence.","contrary_evidence":["Later 2022 nominations of loyal aides and relatives undercut the anti-nepotism and anti-patronage framing."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Leave A Legacy That Will Benefit Others, President Buhari Urges Leaders","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-10-21","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/leave-a-legacy-that-will-benefit-others-president-buhari-urges-leaders/","claim":"Buhari described public service as a public trust, urged accountability, integrity, loyalty, and efficiency, and warned that nepotism, cronyism, patronage, and lack of transparency and accountability distract public officers from their mandate.","locator":"paras. 34-46 of the press release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_low","source_confidence_reason":"Official speech transcript; good evidence of public ethical framing, weak as evidence of actual conduct.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari statement; no independent validation of implementation in this item.","contrary_evidence":["The same year saw criticism of family-linked and loyalist appointments, which complicates the sincerity of the anti-nepotism messaging."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari’s Address at the 2nd National Tax Dialogue Week","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-03-29","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buharis-address-at-the-2nd-national-tax-dialogue/","claim":"Buhari promised continued commitment to the rule of law, transparency, accountability, and prudent management of collective resources at the National Tax Dialogue.","locator":"paras. 12-13 / lines 44-45","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_low","source_confidence_reason":"Official speech transcript; useful for public commitment, but self-report.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari statement.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is aspirational and not by itself proof of honest administration practice."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nigeria’s Buhari asks ministers with political ambition to resign","publisher":"Al Jazeera / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-05-11","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/5/11/nigerias-buhari-asks-ministers-with-political-ambition-to-resign","claim":"Buhari directed cabinet members contesting elective office to resign by May 16, 2022 so they would not unfairly benefit from their government positions.","locator":"lines 67-69","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-syndicated report on a concrete directive and resulting resignations; strong for the fact of the rule, not for motive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 during the election-cycle conflict-of-interest window.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari directive through his information minister; strong nexus to control of office and conflict separation.","contrary_evidence":["The rule covered ministers only, not all appointees, so it did not eliminate broader patronage risks."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.8","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari’s Speech at the Valedictory Session for Appointees Leaving the Cabinet to Pursue Political Ambition","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-05-13","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buharis-speech-at-the-valedictory-session-for-appointees-leaving-the-cabinet-to-pursue-political-ambition/","claim":"Buhari said cabinet selection went through a careful process so that the best and most competent could emerge and described the departure of ministers as managed with dignity and honour.","locator":"lines 30-32 of the speech","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_low","source_confidence_reason":"Official transcript; direct evidence of stated criteria, not independent proof of appointments actually being merit-based.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari statement about his own appointment process and standards.","contrary_evidence":["Later reporting on family-linked and loyalist appointments weakens the claim that competence alone drove selections."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nigeria: Buhari has no preferred successor, spokesman says","publisher":"Al Jazeera / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-06-07","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/6/7/nigerias-buhari-has-no-preferred-successor-spokesman-says","claim":"Reuters reported that Buhari had no preferred APC successor and had anointed no one, and that he would step down in 2023 after eight years in office.","locator":"lines 68-73","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on a specific public statement by the president's spokesman; strong for the public commitment itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 ahead of the succession contest.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Buhari through his spokesman; evidence supports a public non-anointment commitment, not hidden internal intent.","contrary_evidence":["The statement does not prove he exerted no behind-the-scenes influence, only that he denied having a preferred candidate."],"lenses":["7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Buhari's actions contradict nepotism comment","publisher":"Businessday NG","publication_date":"2022-11-02","url":"https://businessday.ng/business-economy/article/buharis-actions-contradict-nepotism-comment/","claim":"The article says Buhari had appointed several family members and close relatives, and specifically notes that in September 2022 Ahmed Halilu, Aisha Buhari's brother, was appointed managing director of the Nigerian Security Printing and Minting Company.","locator":"lines 82-90 of the article","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Published commentary with a concrete appointment and family tie; the underlying appointment is corroborable, though the article is not a formal finding of illegality.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and tied to Buhari's appointing power.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential appointment; strong nexus to Buhari's control over senior posts, though personal enrichment is not shown.","contrary_evidence":["The article acknowledges that the president had constitutional discretion to appoint qualified people, so the appointment alone does not prove corruption or illegality."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Buhari Nominates Lauretta Onochie As NDDC Chair, 14 Other Board Members","publisher":"Channels Television","publication_date":"2022-11-23","url":"https://www.channelstv.com/2022/11/23/buhari-nominates-lauretta-onochie-as-nddc-chair-14-other-board-members/","claim":"Buhari nominated his Special Assistant on Social Media, Lauretta Onochie, as substantive chair of the Niger Delta Development Commission and asked the Senate to confirm the appointment.","locator":"lines 38-42","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of a concrete nomination with clear job history, strong for the appointment fact and loyalty nexus.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari nomination; the appointee was a close political aide, so the loyalty/patronage nexus is strong.","contrary_evidence":["Onochie later denied partisan membership and supporters argued she was qualified, so the nomination is not itself proof of illegality."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Court documents reveal how Lauretta Onochie declared membership of APC under oath","publisher":"The ICIR","publication_date":"2021-06-26","url":"https://www.icirnigeria.org/court-documents-reveal-how-lauretta-onochie-declared-membership-of-apc-under-oath/","claim":"Court documents showed that Lauretta Onochie declared under oath in 2016 that she was a member of the APC and a volunteer at the Buhari Support Organisation, which helped coordinate Buhari's campaigns.","locator":"lines 375-384","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Investigative reporting anchored in court filings; strong for the nominee's partisan history, though retrospective to the 2022 nomination.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Retrospective background used to assess the 2022 nomination of a Buhari aide.","ruler_attribution":"Not Buhari's own statement, but it materially bears on his later choice to nominate a politically partisan aide to an integrity-sensitive post.","contrary_evidence":["Onochie disputed partisan accusations in later proceedings, so the partisan history was contested publicly."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.6","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Senate lied about petition APC nomination as INEC commissioner","publisher":"The ICIR","publication_date":"2022-02-09","url":"https://www.icirnigeria.org/senate-lied-about-petition-against-apc-members-nomination-as-inec-commissioner/","claim":"The ICIR reported that Buhari nominated Rhoda Gumus as an INEC national commissioner despite protests that she was a card-carrying APC member, and that an earlier Onochie nomination had failed after her partisan membership was exposed.","locator":"lines 373-447","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Investigative reporting with contemporaneous confirmation and protest context; strong for the nomination controversy, while allegations of membership remained contested.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in February 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari nomination; the reported partisan-membership controversy makes the loyalty/patronage concern plausible, though not judicially resolved here.","contrary_evidence":["Gumus denied partisan membership and the Senate confirmed her, so the article reflects a contested controversy rather than a finding of illegality."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.6","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Unsubstantiated: Buhari Claim That Ukraine War Feeds Arms to West Africa","publisher":"Voice of America","publication_date":"2022-12-05","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/fact-check-buhari-claim-ukraine-war-feeds-arms-to-west-africa/6863147.html","claim":"Buhari said weapons from the Ukraine-Russia war were beginning to filter into the Lake Chad Basin, but VOA's fact check found the claim unsubstantiated and noted there were no public reports or evidence supporting it.","locator":"lines 98-109","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct quote plus explicit fact-check with sourcing discussion; strong for the unsupported-claim assessment, weaker on intent.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in December 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari public statement; the fact check challenges the claim's evidentiary basis but cannot prove deliberate deception.","contrary_evidence":["There is independent evidence of regional arms diversion from stockpiles and battlefield capture, but not of the specific Ukraine-to-Lake-Chad route Buhari asserted."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I reviewed roughly 30 documents across State House releases, Reuters/Al Jazeera, VOA fact-checking, BusinessDay, Channels, ICIR, Guardian, Punch, Daily Trust, and related follow-up reporting.
- I retained 11 new non-duplicative source-claim units and 2 reused chapter items that directly bear on 7B commitments.
- I rejected duplicate coverage of the same appointment controversies, 2023/2024 items outside the target year, and generic corruption, security, or political-freedom reporting that did not establish a direct Buhari personal-integrity nexus.
- I also excluded fake-news debunks about Buhari’s death or fabricated tweets because they do not show Buhari’s own conduct.
- I treated country-level corruption indicators only as context; they were not used as personal-integrity evidence.

**Remaining gaps**
- There is still no direct 2022 evidence of Buhari’s own assets, bribes, campaign finance, or hidden personal financial benefit.
- There is no court, audit, or inquiry finding directly against Buhari himself in 2022; most negative evidence is indirect and comes through patronage-heavy nominations and public statements.
- The strongest gap is independent evidence on whether Buhari personally knew, directed, or benefited from the family- and loyalist-linked appointments.
- More search would help on asset declarations, procurement records, Senate confirmation materials, and any court or audit files tied to the 2022 nominations.
- The record is stronger on favoritism/patronage and weaker on direct self-enrichment or provable deliberate lying.
